# Chapter 1: A New Day

> Claire de Lune - Claude Debussy

    Sea spray splashed against his wrinkled face.  His fingers hazarded to the scar over his eye.  The claws, he remembered.
    Cornellius walked into the cabin where static emanated from a radio.  He sat down in front of the communications array and looked up at a torn picture of an orange cat with x's crossed over its eyes and a knife pinning the picture to the wall.  He growled.
    He listened to the lack of signal for a few minutes before the ship began to rock.  Cornellius ran outside to see a massive storm cloud brewing to the ship's port.  Before he was able to run to the wheel and turn the ship away, a faint blue glow caught his eye.
    "What is that?", his gravelly voice breathed out.
    He turned the ship to face the bow to the left.

